PART A: exact identities (sympy)
 A1. tangent equation and Wronskian gauge lemma
  [OK] p'' = (eta-mu)p' - zeta p   [on O=0]
  [OK] S_phi' = (eta-mu)S_phi + p L2[phi], phi=U   [on O=0]
  [OK] S_phi' = (eta-mu)S_phi + p L2[phi], phi=-p'   [on O=0]
  [OK] S_phi' = (eta-mu)S_phi + p L2[phi], phi=U+c   [on O=0]
  [OK] S_U = Sigma
  [OK] S_{-p'} = Xi
  [OK] L2[U] = K
  [OK] L2[-p'] = W   [on O=0]
  [OK] L2[1] = zeta
  [OK] L2[p] = 0   [on O=0]
 A2. gauge equations (eq:gaugeodes), state forms, eta0, eta1
  [OK] Sigma' = (eta-mu)Sigma + pK   [on O=0]
  [OK] Xi' = (eta-mu)Xi + pW   [on O=0]
  [OK] Sigma' = -mu Sigma + [U(x-y) - p(y-k)]   (identity)
  [OK] Sigma eta0 = eta Sigma + pK   [on O=0]
  [OK] Xi = p'(k-y) + p(x-y)   (identity)
  [OK] Xi' = x Sigma - A Xi + k psi p'   (identity)
  [OK] (log Xi)' = eta1 - mu   (identity)
  [OK] eta - eta1 = -pW/Xi   [on O=0]
  [OK] Sigma_c' = (eta-mu)Sigma_c + p(K + c zeta)   [on O=0]
  [OK] K' + (1+eta)K = k psi(U)   (identity)
  [OK] W' + (1+eta)W = x p^2   [on O=0]
 A3. scalar reduction (prop:kappa)
  [OK] eta = eta0 - p kappa   [on O=0]
  [OK] zeta = zeta0 - p' kappa   [on O=0]
  [OK] kappa' = k psi/Sigma - (1+eta+eta0-mu) kappa   (identity)
  [OK] kappa' = k psi/Sigma - (1+2eta0-mu)kappa + p kappa^2   [on O=0]
  [OK] W as a function of (eta,zeta)
  [OK] W(eta0-p kappa, zeta0-p' kappa) = W(eta0,zeta0) + kappa Xi   (identity in kappa)
  [OK] K(eta0-p kappa, zeta0-p' kappa) = kappa Sigma   (identity in kappa)
  [OK] kappa=0 plane contains the tangent: zeta0 p - eta0 p' = x-y
  [OK] (Sigma, Sigma eta0, Xi)' = C(.) + k psi (0,p,p')   (identity)
  [OK] eta0' - [zeta0 + (mu-1)eta0 - eta0^2] = k psi p/Sigma
  [OK] zeta0' - [x - (1+eta0)zeta0] = k psi p'/Sigma
  [OK] Delta = [zeta0 dU - eta0 dp - dy] + kappa1 (p1 dp - p1' dU)
  [OK] second point E: bracket vanishes, Delta = -kappa1 Sigma1
 A4. polar form (prop:polar, prop:nestedradii)
  [OK] p' = -r(mu sin + s)
  [OK] r'/r = sin(cos - mu sin - s)
  [OK] theta' = -(sin^2 + mu sin cos + s cos)
  [OK] Sigma = r^2 sigma
  [OK] s' = [k(e^{r cos}-1) - r s]/r - s sin(cos - mu sin - s)
  [OK] dlog r/dtheta = g(s,theta)
  [OK] g(s2)-g(s1) = sin (s2-s1)/(sigma1 sigma2)
  [OK] dg/ds = sin/sigma^2
 A5. Lotka-Volterra chain and second-order forms (prop:lvchain)
  [OK] r1' = r1(lambda+1-r1-ell)
  [OK] r2' = r2(mu-1+r1-r2)
  [OK] ell' = ell(r2-mu)
  [OK] L[eta] = x
  [OK] L[y/ell] = x(A+p)/ell
  [OK] (y/ell)' = x/ell + (mu-1)y/ell - (y/ell)^2  (first Riccati equation, exact)
  [OK] (x/ell)' - [x - (1+y/ell)x/ell] = x(A+2p-lambda)/ell
  [OK] L[phi'/phi + c - 1] = (D+c)(D+c-1)(D+c-mu)phi/phi
  [OK] eta' = omega - G_mu(eta)
  [OK] omega' = x - f_mu(eta)
 A6. strong-stable identities and the comparison lemma (prop:strongidentity, lem A0)
  [OK] (a,-b,-c) solves delta' = J delta
  [OK] a''' + A a'' + mu a' + x a = 0
  [OK] nu = e^{At}(c,b,a) solves nu' = -C^T nu
  [OK] omega^Y=(ell,y,x): omega' - C omega = (0,0,x(2p+A-lambda))
  [OK] omega^c=(1,mu,mu): omega' - C omega = (0,0,kH - x)
  [OK] frak r' = r^2 - mu r - s
  [OK] frak s' = s r - s - x
  [OK] (frak s + r^2/2 - r)' = chi(r) - x
  [OK] r'' + (A-3r) r' + chi(r) = x
  [OK] v = c-(1-mu)b: v' = -mu v - x a
  [OK] (b-a)' = -v
  [OK] chi(s) = s^3 - A s^2 + mu s
  [OK] omega = phi(1,eta~,zeta~): omega' = C omega + diag(g) omega
  [OK] g2 = g1 + R1/eta~
  [OK] g3 = g1 + R2/zeta~
  [OK] true pair: g2 = mu - eta
  [OK] true pair: g3 = mu - eta
  [OK] wedge of two variational solutions: w' = C w
  [OK] wedge(z', z-E) = (Sigma, Sigma eta0, Xi)
  [OK] gamma(gamma-1)(gamma-mu) = f_mu(gamma-1)
 A7. formulas added at the audit (remarks, intermediate proof steps, shifted centre)
  [OK] (p/U)' = -Sigma/U^2
  [OK] (p'/p)' = -Xi/p^2
  [OK] (y-zeta)' + (y-zeta) = eta zeta
  [OK] (ell-eta)' + mu(ell-eta) = (y-zeta) + eta(eta+1-2mu)
  [OK] proof of (gau:Xistate): x Sigma - A Xi + k psi p' = x p^2 + A(p p'' - p'^2) - (x-k)p'
  [OK] proof of (gau:Xistate): Xi' = (p'+mu p)p'' + x p^2 - p(x-y)
  [OK] p'' + A p' + x - k = -mu p   and   p'' + (x-y) = -mu p'
  [OK] (Sigma eta0)' = U[xp-(x-y)] - p'(y-k)
  [OK] kappa-coefficient of W: p[(1+eta0)p' + p zeta0] + p'[p' + (mu-1)p - 2 eta0 p] = Xi
  [OK] zeta0 U - eta0 p - y + k = 0
  [OK] f_mu'' = 6s+4-2mu,  G_mu' = 3s+2-mu,  chi'' = 6s-2A
  [OK] (D+mu)ell = y, (D+1)y = x, (D+A)x = x(p+A)
  [OK] phi=ell, c=A: phi'/phi + c - 1 = y/ell
  [OK] a'' = mu b + c,  a''' = -mu^2 b - A c - x a
  [OK] shifted centre (-c,0): Sigma_c = r^2 sigma
  [OK] shifted centre: theta' = -sigma
  [OK] shifted centre: (log r)' = sin(cos - mu sin - s)
  [OK] shifted centre: K + c zeta = r(zeta cos - eta sin) - (y-k)
  [OK] polar exponent: pK/Sigma = K sin/(r sigma)  (so that dt = -dtheta/sigma gives K sin/(r sigma^2))
  [OK] Lemma gau:wronskian for arbitrary f, g and arbitrary coefficients eta(t), zeta(t): V' = (eta-mu)V + f L2[g] - g L2[f]
  [OK] mixed gauge: S' = (eta-mu)S + pN for S = (1-th)Sigma + th Xi, N = (1-th)K + th W   [on O=0]
  [OK] (p1,p1') wedge (E - q1) = -Sigma1

PART B: floating-point spot checks (whlib cycles; DOP853; averages by periodic trapezoid rule)

